  "order": 71,
  "url": "/css/css_z-index.asp",
  "title": "CSS The z-index Property",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "CSS The z-index Property"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The CSS z-index Property"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The z-index property specifies the stack order of\npositioned elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The stack order defines which element should be placed in front or behind other\nelements."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "When elements are positioned, they can overlap other elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "An element can have a positive or negative stack order (z-index):"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_tree.png",
      "alt": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "This is a heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Because the image has a z-index of -1, it will be placed behind the text."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "img\n{\n\nposition: absolute;\n\n  left: 0px;\n\ntop: 0px;\n\nz-index: -1;\n\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_zindex"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Note:\nz-index only works on positioned elements (position: absolute,\nposition: relative, position: fixed, or position: sticky) and flex items\n(elements that are direct children of display: flex elements)."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Another z-index Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A positioned element with a greater stack order is always above an element\nwith a lower stack order."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<html>\n<head>\n<style>\n.container {\n  position: relative;\n}\n\n.black-box {\n  position: relative;\n  z-index: 1;\n\n  border: 2px solid black;\n  height: 100px;\n  margin: 30px;\n}\n\n.gray-box {\n\n  position: absolute;\n  z-index: 3;\n  background: lightgray;\n  height: 60px;\n\n  width: 70%;\n  left: 50px;\n  top: 50px;\n}\n\n.green-box {\n  position: absolute;\n  z-index: 2;\n  background: lightgreen;\n\n  width: 35%;\n  left: 270px;\n  top: -15px;\n  height:\n  100px;\n}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<div class=\"container\">\n  <div\n  class=\"black-box\">Black box</div>\n  <div class=\"gray-box\">Gray\n  box</div>\n  <div class=\"green-box\">Green box</div>\n</div>\n\n</body>\n</html>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_zindex2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Without z-index"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "If several positioned elements overlap each other without a\nz-index\nspecified, the elements render in the order they are defined in the HTML source\ncode."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<html>\n<head>\n<style>\n.container {\n  position: relative;\n}\n\n.black-box {\n  position: relative;\n\n  border: 2px solid black;\n  height: 100px;\n  margin: 30px;\n}\n\n.gray-box {\n\n  position: absolute;\n  background: lightgray;\n  height: 60px;\n\n  width: 70%;\n  left: 50px;\n  top: 50px;\n}\n\n.green-box {\n  position: absolute;\n  background: lightgreen;\n\n  width: 35%;\n  left: 270px;\n  top: -15px;\n  height:\n  100px;\n}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<div class=\"container\">\n  <div\n  class=\"black-box\">Black box</div>\n  <div class=\"gray-box\">Gray\n  box</div>\n  <div class=\"green-box\">Green box</div>\n</div>\n\n</body>\n</html>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_zindex3"
    },
    {
